Clamp the yuv2rgb_X_c table indices to the table range.

yuv2rgb_X_c_template() (libswscale/output.c) indexes table_rV/gU/gV/bU with U/V and the
luma tables with Y1/Y2. User SwsFilters (sws_getDefaultFilter() blur, sharpen and chroma
shift, which target_sws_fuzzer feeds since 5253641e62) give vertical taps far outside
[0, 4096], and hScale does not clip negative samples, so the sums overshoot the 512-entry
headroom: out-of-bounds pointer reads, then wild reads in yuv2rgb_write() (ASan SEGV /
heap-buffer-overflow; wasm HeapOutOfBounds) for every packed RGB target. Clamp U/V to the
table and Y to +-512 when out of range; the tables saturate inside that range, so in-range
output is unchanged. Adds libswscale/tests/yuv2rgb_overshoot.c (fate-sws-yuv2rgb-overshoot,
fails under ASan without the fix).
Not fixed upstream as of 224205649a.

Upstream: none found (code.ffmpeg.org issues/PRs searched for yuv2rgb, sws_getDefaultFilter).

diff --git a/libswscale/Makefile b/libswscale/Makefile
index 4bd5ff551b..236d39b19c 100644
--- a/libswscale/Makefile
+++ b/libswscale/Makefile
@@ -55,5 +55,6 @@ TESTPROGS = colorspace                                                  \
             sws_ops                                                     \
             sws_ops_aarch64                                             \
